#
# Counter-example for the piecewise gate: a math:PiecewiseFunction that declares its
# math:domain and math:codomain (so the inherited function frame is satisfied and does
# NOT fire) but names NO math:hasPiece (sh:minCount 1). A piecewise function is defined
# BY its pieces; one with none says nothing about what it computes and is ill-formed.
# Every other role is present, so ONLY the missing-piece violation fires. Validation
# MUST emit shacl.MinCountConstraintComponent and NO other finding
# (math:UnderspecifiedPiecewiseFunction). Bound by ex:ecPiecewiseNoPieces.
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:emptyPiecewise a math:PiecewiseFunction ;
    math:domain math:realNumbers ;
    math:codomain math:realNumbers .
